 "title": "Synchronization Overview",
 "summary_for_reviewer": "The synchronization process is designed to ensure that local data is only deleted after successful uploads to the server. If any part of the upload fails, the local data remains intact for future attempts. However, logging out while offline will result in the loss of any unsent data. There are uncertainties regarding how the app handles re-posting run headers after failures and the status of pending runs if a checklist is deleted by an administrator.",
